    clk: qcom: mmcc-msm8974: Propagate VFE AXI rate requests
    
    The VFE AXI branch is sourced by mmss_axi_clk_src, but it does not pass
    rate requests to that parent. The current CCF rounding path consequently
    returns the branch's existing rate. This prevents the new MSM8226 CAMSS
    resource table from raising multimedia AXI bandwidth while streaming.
    
    Set CLK_SET_RATE_PARENT for the VFE AXI branch. Keep its source, gating
    and halt configuration unchanged. In a host fixture using the actual
    CCF rounding function and a table-backed parent, an MSM8226 request for
    266.67 MHz now reaches the parent and selects 266666666 Hz instead of
    retaining the 100 MHz starting rate. Parent errors propagate, and an
    omitted-flag control retains the old result.
    
    This enables the new CAMSS platform configuration; it does not claim a
    newly introduced upstream capture regression. The integration's earlier
    full-frame result is historical. No hardware or full CCF rate-change
    acceptance is inherited on this base.
    
    Original integration work by Timothy Schmidt credits Claude Opus 5.5
    <noreply@anthropic.com> as co-author. This current-base refresh and host
    qualification used OpenAI Codex. Human review and DCO remain pending.

